# .env.example -- versioned template. Copy to .env (git-ignored) on each machine.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && $EDITOR .env
#
# .env holds ONLY what is private or machine-specific in a way that must not be
# published: the project code and the absolute paths. Everything that is merely
# machine-dependent but harmless -- number of workers, pinning -- belongs in
# configs/site/*.yaml, where YAML types it and git records it.
#
# Every key listed here must exist in .env: slurm/preflight.sh compares the two files
# and fails on any key present here and missing there. Add a key here when you add one
# to the code, so that other machines are told about it instead of failing at run time.

# --- IDRIS project code, 3 letters, WITHOUT the @v100 suffix (`idrproj`).
# Leave empty on a machine with no Slurm.
JZ_PROJECT=

# --- Absolute path to the datasets root.
# torchvision expects <root>/cifar-10-batches-py and <root>/MNIST/raw.
# Jean Zay: $DSDIR
GRNEWT_DATASETS=

# --- Absolute path to the results root.
# Jean Zay: use $SCRATCH (large quotas, purged after 30 days) or $WORK (backed up,
# limited inode quota). NEVER $STORE: it is unreachable from the compute nodes since
# 2024-07-22, and a job whose --output points there dies without writing any log.
GRNEWT_RESULTS=
